                "answer": "C",
                "explanation": "<strong>C</strong> <p>The normal line is\r                                 perpendicular to the tangent line at the point of tangency, and\r                                 perpendicular lines have negative reciprocal slopes. The slope of\r                                 the tangent line is <img src=\"images/1317970d46fa4af08e43ee613ebe9aeb.png\" class=\"exam-img\" style=\"max-width:100%; vertical-align:middle; margin:4px 0;\">, so the slope of the normal line must be <img src=\"images/43c9cce75823462d91afb99ffac6329a.png\" class=\"exam-img\" style=\"max-width:100%; vertical-align:middle; margin:4px 0;\">. Because <img src=\"images/145f7db234df4943b8c6ddd52cb36d49.png\" class=\"exam-img\" style=\"max-width:100%; vertical-align:middle; margin:4px 0;\"> is tangent to <em>f</em>(<em>x</em>) at <em>x</em> = 3, you can\r                                 find <em>f</em>(3) by evaluating <em>y</em>(3).</p> <p><img src=\"images/832307ab049d463a8f50f513b033d949.png\" class=\"exam-img\" style=\"max-width:100%; vertical-align:middle; margin:4px 0;\"></p> <p>The point (3, 7) and the\r                                 slope <img src=\"images/e4e64204e355460bb0c32381b03532d3.png\" class=\"exam-img\" style=\"max-width:100%; vertical-align:middle; margin:4px 0;\"> can now be put into the point-slope form of a line.</p> <p><img src=\"images/213dbf6ff624481b869898f129a2b360.png\" class=\"exam-img\" style=\"max-width:100%; vertical-align:middle; margin:4px 0;\"></p> <p>Thus, (C) is correct.\r                                 (A) uses the reciprocal slope of the tangent line instead of the\r                                 negative reciprocal. (B) uses the correct slope but incorrectly\r                                 distributes the slope when working with the point-slope form of a\r                                 line.</p>"
