                "answer": "A",
                "explanation": "<strong>A</strong> <p>The <em>u</em>-value is\r                                 provided, and <img src=\"images/6b03ec24f32e42e79a3b95e33e387321.png\" class=\"exam-img\" style=\"max-width:100%; vertical-align:middle; margin:4px 0;\">. Substituting <em>u</em> for <img src=\"images/91cccc24f96f4d4d9ee6c8d8006ae540.png\" class=\"exam-img\" style=\"max-width:100%; vertical-align:middle; margin:4px 0;\"> in the numerator leaves <img src=\"images/3f909d00331a4dca9ec6877a6bc922c8.png\" class=\"exam-img\" style=\"max-width:100%; vertical-align:middle; margin:4px 0;\">. Solving <img src=\"images/e3816de2230245758ed3da3952bee068.png\" class=\"exam-img\" style=\"max-width:100%; vertical-align:middle; margin:4px 0;\"> for <em>x</em> allows you to replace the <em>x</em> in the\r                                 denominator with 3<em>u</em>, making the new integral <img src=\"images/e2fefe1fe76c43c9a32fa4faa3305606.png\" class=\"exam-img\" style=\"max-width:100%; vertical-align:middle; margin:4px 0;\">. Because <img src=\"images/ec0270bb8a294cc08aa4a6c610c03afd.png\" class=\"exam-img\" style=\"max-width:100%; vertical-align:middle; margin:4px 0;\">, it replaces the <em>dx</em> and the 3 in the denominator when\r                                 substituted, <img src=\"images/08326c857abe4db783a6a3c1b9aad4df.png\" class=\"exam-img\" style=\"max-width:100%; vertical-align:middle; margin:4px 0;\">. The upper and lower bounds need to be adjusted to make them\r                                 in terms of <em>u</em>, which means they both need to be divided by 3.\r                                 The definite integral to be evaluated is now <img src=\"images/da4f6f8699144f20a049f4f1a16781be.png\" class=\"exam-img\" style=\"max-width:100%; vertical-align:middle; margin:4px 0;\"> or <img src=\"images/187de0d85e724a7f97406b211ba3f2af.png\" class=\"exam-img\" style=\"max-width:100%; vertical-align:middle; margin:4px 0;\">. The antiderivative of <img src=\"images/685eb4ed19f24b38895ac64b4b15ed82.png\" class=\"exam-img\" style=\"max-width:100%; vertical-align:middle; margin:4px 0;\"> is <img src=\"images/d9b2442ab1d54be99447cedf690df696.png\" class=\"exam-img\" style=\"max-width:100%; vertical-align:middle; margin:4px 0;\">, and the power rule can be applied to <em>u</em>.</p> <p><img src=\"images/fcd9f9e549864603a9b1bf2ce978069b.png\" class=\"exam-img\" style=\"max-width:100%; vertical-align:middle; margin:4px 0;\"></p> <p>Hence, (A) is correct.\r                                 If you got (B), you ignored the <em>x</em> in the denominator of the\r                                 original function. C) contains an algebraic error when subtracting\r                                 the results after substituting the upper and lower bound values. (D)\r                                 is a result of forgetting to adjust the upper and lower bound\r                                 values.</p>"
