                "answer": "A",
                "explanation": "<strong>A</strong> <p>Using the identity\r                                     sin<sup>2</sup><em>x</em> + cos<sup>2</sup><em>x</em> = 1, evaluate\r                                     <img src=\"images/68a6b50d8f09419e8d4cddae01fd87c4.png\" class=\"exam-img\" style=\"max-width:100%; vertical-align:middle; margin:4px 0;\">. So you need to find the reciprocal of tan <img src=\"images/98cabe3f1cc240cfafb4bd23f6e7549a.png\" class=\"exam-img\" style=\"max-width:100%; vertical-align:middle; margin:4px 0;\">, which is <img src=\"images/246baaf47c8b4086b96553afefd901eb.png\" class=\"exam-img\" style=\"max-width:100%; vertical-align:middle; margin:4px 0;\"> .</p> <p>Therefore, the correct\r                                 answer is <img src=\"images/8423a467ace24510a111463cc3285412.png\" class=\"exam-img\" style=\"max-width:100%; vertical-align:middle; margin:4px 0;\">, matching (A). (B), although tempting, is the <img src=\"images/c4fe1b825e464474a04a9dcbfca879f7.png\" class=\"exam-img\" style=\"max-width:100%; vertical-align:middle; margin:4px 0;\"> . (C) ignores the 2 in the tangent function and the\r                                 reciprocal; it is the <img src=\"images/3269ff82f0da4b99b596817bc46cda66.png\" class=\"exam-img\" style=\"max-width:100%; vertical-align:middle; margin:4px 0;\">. (D) ignores the necessary squares on the sine and cosine\r                                 functions.</p>"
