                "answer": "C",
                "explanation": "<strong>C</strong>  <p>Graph the given\r                                     functions to visualize which function is on top and which is on\r                                     the bottom. The graph also allows you to locate the\r                                     <em>x</em>-value where <em>y</em> = sin <em>x</em> and <em>y</em> =\r                                         –<em>x</em> + 3 intersect, which is the upper bound of the\r                                     definite integral. Because sin <em>x</em> = –<em>x</em> + 3 at\r                                         <em>x</em> = 2.180 and the linear function is the top\r                                     function, the definite integral is <img src=\"images/b3e7fde43d724599b6bb80b57949754d.png\" class=\"exam-img\" style=\"max-width:100%; vertical-align:middle; margin:4px 0;\">. Once again, there is no reason to take the\r                                     antiderivative because the calculator can evaluate this definite\r                                     integral for you. The area is 2.592, which is (C).</p> <p>(A) is just the area\r                                     under the sine function. (B) is the <em>x</em>-coordinate of the\r                                     point of intersection, which needs to be used as a bound. (D) is\r                                     the area under the linear function on the same interval.</p>"
