                "topic": "Section I: Part B (Calculator Active)",
                "difficulty": "hard",
                "question": "<p>The function <em>f</em> is defined by <em>f</em>(<em>x</em>) = 4<em>x</em> – 3 sin(2<em>x</em> + 1), and its derivative is <em>f</em><em>′</em>(<em>x</em>) = 4 – 6 cos(2<em>x</em> + 1). What are all values of <em>x</em> that satisfy the conclusion of the mean value theorem applied to <em>f</em> on the closed interval [–1, 2] ?</p>",
